steps.brief:
Files: packages/hub/src/hub.ts, landings.ts (new: queueLanding, positionOf, etaOf, landed-effects and failure-effects helpers), holds.ts (new: setHolds, holdsToLeases, releaseHolds, moveHolds). Read DESIGN 1.4 (T0, T1, T14, T15), 1.6 and 2.1. Build:
(1) land() dispatch. land() without queue keeps the Phase 1 body, but answers 409 landing_queue_active once any claim on LANDER_LEASE_KEY (from @agenthub/contract) has existed, whatever its status. land() with queue:true calls queueLanding, which runs in one durable write:
  - validate FULL_SHA_RE (400 bad_commit), files via normalizeRepoPath (at most 20000), scope via normalizeScope with mapper, and summary via cleanText (at most 4000);
  - replay: a live landing of the same (agent, commit) comes back with replayed: true;
  - Phase 1 task rules (403, task_closed, task_blocked);
  - predecessor: the same (agent, task), or (agent, branch) without a task. In phase pushing it is 409 too_late; if it is live, supersede it (superseded_by set, holds moved, queue_seq inherited);
  - retry chain: the agent's latest failed landing of the task in the last 24 h sets retry_of and retry+1; inherit queue_seq while retry <= control.policy.keep_place_retries, otherwise take a new value from the counter landing-queue;
  - setHolds over the advisory entries plus the entries of the claims selected by the Phase 1 land rule, with the gate from control.policy.claim_gate. fail means 409 claim_conflict with details.conflicts and nothing created; warn leaves the conflicting entries out. The selected claims end with endClaim reason 'moved to landing L-n';
  - task goes to landing (owner = agent); insert status submitted; emit landing.created;
  - return LandResult with held, superseded, replayed, position, eta_ms, lander and a hub-written note.
(2) setHolds per 1.6: normalize; find other agents' active overlapping claims with overlappingEntries (mapper gating); choose shared or exclusive per entry by the auto rule; gate; create or rescope at most two hold rows (holder = agent, landing_id, task_id, intent 'landing L-n: <title>', expires_at HOLD_EXPIRES), emitting claim.granted with landing_id, or a partial claim.released for trimmed entries; release entries no longer in scope and run promoteQueued.
(3) renewLeases sets expires_at = Math.max(expires_at, now + ttl_ms).
(4) In claim(), the coverage set mine excludes holds. clash still compares holders, so the agent's own hold never blocks it.
(5) release: a hold's claim_id gives 409 held_by_landing; all, task_id and files skip holds.
(6) In buildWaits, Reach and waitCycle, a hold's node is 'landing:'+landing_id instead of its holder.
(7) check() counts other agents' holds as exclusive conflicts. toConflict fills scope (the overlapping entries) and landing_id.
(8) takeTask and updateTask refuse a task in landing with 409 task_landing. resolveTaskId counts in_progress only.
(9) Helpers for H3. Landed effects: releaseHolds with reason 'landed L-n', promoteQueued, task done plus announceUnblocked. Failure effects: holdsToLeases with landing_id null and expires_at = now + max(ttl_ms, sendback_grace_min), and the task back to in_progress.
Acceptance tests (holds.test.ts and landings.queue.test.ts, fake clock): bad_commit; replay; task rules; supersede moves the holds and inherits queue_seq; too_late when the predecessor is pushing (set it up through the store); the retry chain inherits queue_seq for 2 retries, then gets a new value; the advisory gate gives 409 claim_conflict with details.conflicts and creates no landing or hold; warn mode proceeds; a hold survives a 1-day clock jump; heartbeat renewed counts holds and never shortens them; the holder's new claim on a held file is a separate lease that survives releaseHolds; held_by_landing; no false deadlock (agent A with a hold on X queues for Y held by B, while B waits for X); a guard check by a third agent sees A's hold; all Phase 1 land tests pass in record mode while no lander has ever existed; record mode gives 409 landing_queue_active after a lander lease claim was ever made.

Files: packages/hub/src/landings.ts, lander-control.ts (new), hub.ts. Read DESIGN 1.4 (all of T2 to T16), 1.5 and 2.1. Every method takes auth: {lander: boolean, approver: string | null}, which the server computes in H4; tests pass it directly. Build:
(1) Reserved key: claim() refuses entries under RESERVED_PREFIX unless auth.lander is true and the scope is exactly [LANDER_LEASE_KEY] in exclusive mode (403 forbidden).
(2) assertLander(project, agent, lease): runs inside write() after expireDue. Requires an active claim with id lease.lease_claim_id on LANDER_LEASE_KEY, held by agent, and epoch == store.epoch(). Otherwise 409 not_lander.
(3) endClaim calls onLeaseEnded when the ended claim is on LANDER_LEASE_KEY. That lease's running landing goes to queued (T9 lander_lost; retries.lander_lost+1; past 3 it fails with lander_lost) or, if its phase is pushing, gets in_doubt = true (T10).
(4) nextLanding (T4): an in-doubt landing, or the caller's own running landing, comes first with resolve set (this also works while paused). Otherwise, unless paused, take the lowest-queue_seq queued landing whose waits_for is null or terminal: set running, phase merging, attempt+1, lander, lease_claim_id, started_at, deadline 10 min.
(5) admitLanding (T2/T3): the landing must be submitted; otherwise the call is a replay. Run setHolds with the exact scope and the gate (fail gives status failed, code claim_conflict). approval = required minus approvals with the same kind and digest found along the retry_of and supersedes chain (copy them into landing_approvals with carried_from). If anything is still pending, emit landing.needs_approval with parked false.
(6) advanceLanding, fenced and attempt-checked (409 landing_stale); a request already reflected in the row answers replayed: true:
  - phase changes, with deadline_ms clamped to 1 min to 6 h and first_base set from trunk_base;
  - entering pushing needs candidate, candidate_ref, tree and trunk_base, and every requirement in required satisfied by a granted approval (409 approval_missing with details.missing). This write is durable and deadline_at becomes null;
  - needs_approval (T6): candidate_checked true, approval = required, deadline_at = now + approval_timeout_hours, slot freed;
  - queued (T9) with the retry limits: trunk_moved 3 then failed trunk_busy, step_timeout 2 then failed lander_stuck; lander_stopping is not counted;
  - landed (T11): landed effects, also_landed annotated with landed_with, control.trunk set, events landing.landed and trunk.moved with foreign false;
  - failed (T13): failure effects.
(7) resolveLanding (T11/T12): only for an in-doubt or own pushing landing. landed applies the landed effects; requeue keeps queue_seq and counts trunk_moved.
(8) approveLanding and rejectLanding (T7/T8). A digest that matches no pending requirement gives 409 approval_stale. Rule checks: approvers lists and distinct (approver != humanOf(agent)), otherwise 403 not_approver naming the rule. Append a landing_approvals row. When nothing is pending and the status is needs_approval, go back to queued with the same queue_seq.
(9) cancelLanding (T14): author or approver; 409 too_late in pushing; 409 landing_closed when terminal.
(10) expireLandings in the write pre-step and in read()'s due check: step_timeout requeue and approval_timeout failure.
(11) reportTrunk: sets control.trunk and control.policy. rewritten sets the pause trunk_rewritten and emits lander.paused. Each reported commit whose trailers (landing, hub == epoch, source == landing.commit) match a non-landed landing is reconciled to landed (T16, reconciled true, landed effects as far as they still apply). Commits that match nothing produce trunk.moved with foreign true. Also pause and resume (resume optionally takes accept_trunk).
(12) status() fills queue, lander and control. landingStats computes per-chain median and p90 land-to-trunk, first_try_rate, sendbacks, median check and median queue wait.
Acceptance tests (landings.lander.test.ts and lander-lease.test.ts, fake clock):
  - every T2 to T16 row and guard;
  - not_lander after expiry, before the sweeper runs; epoch mismatch; landing_stale after cancel, supersede and requeue;
  - in_doubt is never requeued by the sweep, by time or by lease loss; resolve requeue keeps queue_seq; a duplicate advance landed answers replayed: true;
  - approval_missing; approval while queued; parked resume keeps queue_seq; carry-over; distinct; two rules needing two humans;
  - T16 reconcile of a cancelled landing; rewritten pauses; next returns only in-doubt landings while paused;
  - LandingStats on a synthetic history;
  - two OS processes racing the lease claim on one database file give exactly one active claim (reuse test/fixtures/race-child.mjs).

Files: packages/hub/src/server.ts, cli.ts, index.ts. Read DESIGN 1.2 (flags), 1.7 and 6.3.7. Build:
(1) Every section 1.7 route in buildRoutes. Put /landings/stats before /landings/:id.
(2) Auth from headers. lander: x-hub-agent starts with lander/ and x-hub-lander-token matches --lander-token (timingSafeEqual); without a configured token, lander routes are allowed only when the bound address is loopback, otherwise 403 lander_token_required. approver: x-hub-approver plus x-hub-approver-token, whose sha256 hex must equal the --approvers JSON entry ('sha256:<hex>'); with no file, 403 approvals_disabled; with --allow-unauthenticated-approvals (loopback only) the name alone is enough. Pass auth into the Hub methods.
(3) sendError includes details. HubError gains an optional details argument.
(4) cli.ts: --lander-token / HUB_LANDER_TOKEN, --approvers FILE / HUB_APPROVERS_FILE (validated JSON), --allow-unauthenticated-approvals (refused with exit 2 and one line when --host is not loopback), all validated before the database opens, as H5 already does for the lease flags. Startup warnings: no lander token, unauthenticated approvals. Log lines name landing_id.
(5) index.ts exports the new public functions.
Acceptance tests (server.landing.test.ts):
  - every route's happy path and each listed error over real HTTP;
  - a hub on 0.0.0.0 without a lander token answers 403 lander_token_required; a wrong token answers 403;
  - a wrong approver token answers 403 not_approver; with no file, approvals_disabled;
  - hub-server --allow-unauthenticated-approvals --host 0.0.0.0 exits 2 with one line;
  - claim_conflict bodies carry details.conflicts;
  - every request fixture in packages/hub/test/fixtures/contract is accepted, and every response shape matches its fixture (same keys and types);
  - a full cycle over HTTP (land, admit, next, advance merging, checking, pushing, landed) emits events in order and releases the holds.

Files: packages/hub/src/hub.ts (and an optional scope.ts helper). Read DESIGN 1.10 and the contract functions entriesOverlap, entryCovers, overlappingEntries, claimCovers and isValidSymbolKey. Build:
(1) normalizeScope validates each symbol with isValidSymbolKey and requires req.mapper when any entry has a symbol (400 invalid_symbol). Store mapper on the claim.
(2) In claim(): coverage uses claimCovers per wanted entry with mapper gating; uncovered becomes a list of entries; others are the live claims whose overlappingEntries against the uncovered entries is non-empty; sameFiles becomes sameScope.
(3) clash(a, b) = holder/mode clash AND overlappingEntries(a, b) is non-empty. near() and byFile() keep indexing by file, as a superset prefilter. leftAlone stays file-based.
(4) release({files}) drops every entry of those files.
(5) check({files?, scope?, mapper?}) compares entries.
(6) toConflict.scope lists the overlapping entries. Claim events carry scope and mapper.
Acceptance tests (symbol-scope.test.ts):
  - disjoint symbols in one file are both granted;
  - the same symbol, container vs member, and file vs symbol are denied, with conflict scope naming the entries;
  - @imports vs @imports is granted;
  - a mapper mismatch, or a null mapper with a symbol, compares at file level;
  - queue promotion works with symbol scopes;
  - seeded property tests: overlap is symmetric, and covers implies overlaps;
  - the Phase 1 race tests (2 and 30 HTTP clients, 6 processes) rerun on a contended symbol grant exactly one;
  - all Phase 1 tests pass unchanged.

Files: packages/gitops/src/index.ts (implement every function of the frozen types.ts GitOps interface; export const gitops and named exports), test/**. Zero npm dependencies. Read DESIGN 1.1, 2.2.2, 2.2.5, 2.2.6 and 6.3.3. Build:
(1) open(dir, {isolated}). isolated adds env GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null, GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1, GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0, HUB_GUARD=off and args -c core.hooksPath=/dev/null -c gc.auto=0 -c merge.conflictStyle=diff3. Lock errors ('Unable to create ... .lock') are retried 3 times with jitter. Fetches use --no-write-fetch-head.
(2) features() probes merge-tree --write-tree -z --merge-base and --attr-source.
(3) mergeTrees runs git --attr-source=<attrSource> merge-tree --write-tree -z --messages --merge-base=<base> and parses the -z output (tree, then mode oid stage TAB path, then the messages block). Stage 2 writes info/attributes from the drivers' patterns and adds -c merge.<name>.name and -c merge.<name>.driver; only paths that conflicted in stage 1 and are clean in stage 2 take stage 2's blob, via spliceTree into stage 1's tree. info/attributes is truncated afterwards.
(4) spliceTree uses a temporary GIT_INDEX_FILE: read-tree, then hash-object -w and update-index --cacheinfo, then write-tree. commitTree takes an explicit author and committer env.
(5) landedBase per DESIGN 1.1. trunkTrailers parses git log --first-parent with %(trailers:key=...,valueonly). findLandingCommit requires the Landing, Hub and Source trailers all to match. sanitizeMessageText strips TRAILER_LINE_RE lines and control/bidi characters.
(6) replay loops merge-tree --merge-base=c^ plus commit-tree with the original author and date; a merge commit gives the merges outcome.
(7) forecastConflicts uses merge-tree --name-only. stashCreate runs git stash create.
(8) pushTrunk asserts C^1 == expected and isAncestor(expected, C), then runs exactly git push --atomic --porcelain --force-with-lease=refs/heads/<trunk>:<expected> <remote> <C>:refs/heads/<trunk> [:<deleteRef>]. Classify the result: ok, up_to_date, stale (stale info or non-fast-forward), rejected (remote rejected), or unknown (network error or timeout).
(9) pushRef only accepts refs under <prefix>land/ and <prefix>cand/ and never forces. lsRemote. approvalDigest = sha256 over the sorted lines kind NUL path NUL blobs.
Acceptance tests (packages/gitops/test, real git with testEnv: GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null, fixed author and committer names, emails and dates):
  - the union attack: an incoming .gitattributes with *.ts merge=union does not resolve a conflict under attrSource=T0, while trunk's own attributes do apply;
  - four conflict kinds parsed (content, modify/delete, rename/delete, binary);
  - the fake driver runs only in stage 2, and other files stay byte-identical to stage 1;
  - landedBase vectors: fork point, landed source, reverted landing, stacked commits;
  - a forged trailer line in a summary is stripped, and a non-first-parent trailer is ignored;
  - a recreated-database collision (same landing id, other source or epoch) does not match;
  - pushTrunk: the exact argument list; ok; up_to_date; stale on a moved trunk; stale on a rewound trunk; rejected via an update hook; the land ref deleted atomically; a non-child candidate refused before any push;
  - pushRef refuses a ref outside the allowlist;
  - a replay conflict leaves refs, index and files byte-identical;
  - stashCreate writes no refs and leaves the index and worktree unchanged;
  - approvalDigest vectors.

Files: packages/lander/src/lease.ts, admission.ts, pipeline.ts (written only against ports.ts), trunk.ts, gc.ts, faults.ts, cli.ts, bin/hub-lander.js. Read DESIGN 2.2.1 to 2.2.7 and 2.2.10. Build:
(1) Lease loop: claim LANDER_LEASE_KEY with ttl 60 s and queue:true, as id lander/<host>-<pid>-<4hex>. Standby by heartbeating the queued claim and long-polling claim.granted. Heartbeat every 15 s on a timer that runs during checks. Self-fencing: no advance pushing or trunk push unless the last ack is younger than ttl/3, by both wall and monotonic time. not_lander aborts the in-memory attempt and kills the check.
(2) Admission loop (DESIGN 2.2.4): GET /landings?status=submitted on landing.created events or every 15 s; fetch the land ref and admit-trunk; verify the tip; strict config from trunk (invalid means pause config_invalid); landedBase, diffNames and the size limits; protected requirements with gitops.approvalDigest; containment (waits_for, contains_unlanded); then POST admit.
(3) Attempt loop (DESIGN 2.2.5, P1 to P11): fetch and verify; config from T0; trunk scan via POST /lander/trunk (rewritten means pause and requeue; policy reported); the already-landed check with findLandingCommit; the waits_for resolution; base and protected recheck; the merge ladder stages 1 and 2 (stage 3 behind ResolverPort, where a null resolver means skipped); the no-op case; candidate commitTree with the C^1 assert; merged requirements; the approved fast path; checks with the trunk watch (ls-remote every 15 s); staging failed candidates; parking via advance needs_approval with the candidate staged; the write-ahead (pushRef candidate, then advance pushing with required); pushTrunk with the outcome table (stale means resolve landed or requeue; rejected means pause push_rejected and keep the landing pushing; unknown means retry 5 times, then leave it in doubt); advance landed; direct messages to authors; cleanup.
(4) GC at start and hourly: worktree prune; runs/*; refs per DESIGN 2.2.7.
(5) SIGTERM: kill the check; advance queued lander_stopping, or resolve first if pushing; release the lease.
(6) CLI: init --remote --dir (bare clone, fetch refspecs emptied, credential helper); run [--once]; doctor (one line per check, exit 1 on any failure: git features, push/delete of a probe ref under P cand/doctor/, strict config, structural self-test, hub token, isolation warning).
Acceptance tests (lander.integration.test.ts: a real bare remote with receive.denyNonFastForwards and an update hook that refuses trunk updates whose committer isn't the lander identity, a real hub from CP1a on port 0, run --once or in the background, node check.mjs gated by signal files), every DESIGN 5.3 row except the AI rows:
  - happy path; FIFO across two clones; structural with the fake mergiraf on PATH;
  - checks failed (log_tail, failed_tests, passes_on_trunk, staged candidate); protected approved while queued; protected parked, then approved, then landed with no second check run;
  - merged protected with approval_stale; the claim gate failing a landing that touches another agent's claimed file;
  - trunk moves mid-check (trunk watch); trunk moves between check and push; trunk rewritten (pause, then resume --accept-trunk); push_rejected (landing stays pushing; after resume the same candidate is pushed);
  - no-op; stacked waits_for; contains_unlanded; config invalid on trunk pauses;
  - doctor exits 1 when git lacks a feature (shim git on PATH).

Files: packages/lander/src/recovery.ts, test/simulation.test.ts, test/crash.test.ts, test/fakes/git-port.ts, test/fakes/checks-port.ts. Read DESIGN 2.2.7, 5.2 and 5.4. Build:
(1) Startup recovery: worktree prune, kill the pgids in state.json, remove runs/* and local candidate refs, then resolve in-doubt landings through next.
(2) resolveInDoubt, in order: if the candidate is an ancestor of trunk, or findLandingCommit finds it, resolve landed; else if the tip == trunk_base and the candidate ref resolves to the candidate, pushTrunk the same C; else if trunk moved past trunk_base, or the candidate ref is gone, resolve requeue.
(3) Fault points via AGENTHUB_LANDER_FAULTS (NODE_ENV=test only) that SIGKILL the process: after-admit, after-next, during-merge, during-checks, after-checks, after-candidate-staged, after-pushing-ack, after-trunk-push, before-landed-ack, after-landed-ack.
(4) The simulation: the real pipeline.ts against the real Hub in-process (SqliteStore :memory:, fake clock), a fake GitPort (an in-memory remote with fast-forward-only CAS, candidate refs and trailer-bearing commits), a fake ChecksPort and the stub resolver, under a seeded scheduler. Inject crashes at faults and between awaits, dropped requests and responses, unknown push outcomes, lease expiry by clock jumps, foreign pushes, a rewind plus accept, cancels, supersedes and re-lands, and a second lander. After each step check: lander pushes are fast-forwards from the expected tip whose (parent, tree) passed; no landing's change is on trunk twice; at most one running; landed implies on trunk; cancelled, failed or superseded implies not on trunk unless reconciled; holds are live iff the landing is live. After the faults stop, every landing must reach a terminal state, with the hub and trunk agreeing.
Acceptance tests:
  - crash.test.ts: one test per fault point (child lander killed, a second lander takes over after the 1 s TTL) asserting exactly one trunk commit for the landing, the expected state and retries, and no stray refs after GC;
  - the stale-lander SIGSTOP/SIGCONT test (its writes get not_lander; its push is refused or up_to_date; one trunk commit);
  - a hub-restart test during checking and during pushing;
  - the simulation green on 2,000 seeds (SIM_SEEDS env raises it);
  - each of the 5 mutation guards (plain push with rewinds injected; push before recording pushing; requeue pushing on lease loss; cancel allowed in pushing; trailer match on the landing id only with a recreated database) makes the invariants fail.

Files: packages/adapter/src/config.ts (teamSections(root, {strict}), reading trunk's agenthub.json via git show refs/remotes/<remote>/<trunk>:agenthub.json and falling back to the worktree's, through parseTeamSections; lenient in hooks, where problems become warnings), git.ts (gitDir(root) from the .git file's gitdir line; fullHead), client.ts (the queue-mode land, landings, landing, landingStats, cancel, approve, reject, lander, postSymbolChanges, symbolChanges), land.ts (new), mcp.ts, format.ts, human.ts, cli.ts HELP. Read DESIGN 2.3.1 to 2.3.4, 2.3.7 and 3.7. Build:
(1) The land tool and hub land, in order:
  - identity;
  - refuse a git operation in progress;
  - status --porcelain=v1 -z --untracked-files=all: refuse tracked changes; refuse untracked non-ignored files unless allow_untracked;
  - fetch trunk (10 s; on failure continue with the last fetched trunk and a warning);
  - H = full HEAD; base = gitops.landedBase; files = diffNames; empty means 'nothing to land';
  - preview: merge-tree --name-only conflicts with attribution, protected matches, scope;
  - git push <remote> H:<P>land/H, never forced;
  - POST /land with queue:true and the advisory files, scope, mapper and preview;
  - feed.noteClaims(held); the result texts of DESIGN 2.3.2; optional wait_s.
  Without a land config, use Phase 1 record mode, and explain landing_queue_active when the hub answers with it. If the hub answers status recorded to a queue request (a Phase 1 hub), say that nothing was queued.
(2) landing_status, with the fix-it rendering of DESIGN 2.3.3 (check logs, hunks and others' summaries inside untrustedBlock, the reproduce line, next_steps). land_cancel. hub_wait landing_id wakes on landing events for that landing and returns at once when it is terminal or parked; with no arguments it also wakes on the agent's own landings.
(3) digestText, statusText and the queue view: hide the lander lease claim; show holds as 'being landed by L-n'; formatEvent covers the new events; the INSTRUCTIONS text of DESIGN 2.3.2.
(4) The human CLI: landings [--all] [--watch] [--stats], landing, cancel, approve and reject, lander [resume --accept-trunk], doctor. approve and reject require a TTY on stdin and stdout and read ~/.config/agenthub/approver.json (refused unless 0600) or HUB_APPROVER and HUB_APPROVER_TOKEN. They fetch the land ref or the candidate, show the diff for each pending kind, recompute the digest with gitops.approvalDigest (refusing on a mismatch), ask the human to type the landing id, then post.
Acceptance tests (land.test.ts and landing-ux.test.ts, with a real hub and a bare remote; drive admit and advance directly over HTTP with a test lander token in place of a lander):
  - the land ref is pushed under the exact name and never forced;
  - each refusal (tracked dirty, untracked without allow_untracked, operation in progress, nothing to land) pushes and posts nothing;
  - an idempotent re-call answers replayed;
  - a claim_conflict message labels holder intents as theirs;
  - hub_wait returns on landed and on failed, and at once for a terminal landing;
  - fix-it renderings match snapshots, with untrusted wrapping;
  - hub approve refuses without a TTY and with a 0644 file, and succeeds through a pseudo-TTY;
  - lenient config never throws: a bad land value becomes a digest warning while pre-edit still allows edits.

Files: packages/adapter/src/sync.ts (new), hooks.ts, mcp.ts (hub_sync), human.ts (hub sync), guard.ts (--pre-push), init.ts (install pre-push via guardHooks), feed.ts. Read DESIGN 2.3.4, 2.3.5, 2.3.6 (the Phase 2 parts) and 3.10. Build:
(1) syncWorkspace exactly as the 11-step listing in DESIGN 2.3.5: recover, lock, markers, fetch, git-operation check, the own live landing check, the dirty forecast via gitops.stashCreate and forecastConflicts, the plan via landedBase and gitops.replay, the sync.json write-ahead plus a backup ref refs/agenthub/backup/<branch>/<ms>, the HEAD compare-and-swap with git reset --keep, then verify. Files live under the per-worktree git dir G/agenthub/. There is no reset --hard, checkout -f, clean or stash anywhere.
(2) hub_sync and hub sync with the update and merge modes; merge requires a clean tracked tree, no own live landing in HEAD's history and no inflight markers, then runs git merge --no-edit.
(3) Edit/sync exclusion. preEditHook writes G/agenthub/inflight/<session>~<tool_use_id> first, then checks sync.lock; if it is held, it removes the marker, waits up to 3 s, retries once, then denies 'retry this edit'. postEditHook and settleHook remove markers. If an interrupted sync.json exists, pre-edit denies with 'call hub_sync to finish recovering'.
(4) Safe points: digestHook syncs before building the digest; settleHook syncs on UserPromptSubmit only, after releasing pending claims, and prints additionalContext only when something changed, conflicted or is behind and dirty. Both are bounded at 15 s. sync.auto false disables both.
(5) The stale-base heads-up in pre-edit (merge-base cached per HEAD and trunk in G/agenthub/mergebase).
(6) The feed: notices for own landings, needs_approval for my human, and trunk.moved touching held or modified files; a background git fetch of trunk on landing.landed and trunk.moved.
(7) guard --pre-push refuses updates of refs/heads/<trunk> and <P>cand/*, with HUB_GUARD=off as the bypass. init installs and chains pre-push like the other guard scripts.
Acceptance tests (sync.test.ts and pre-push.test.ts, real repositories):
  - clean and fully landed resets to trunk; clean with unlanded commits replays them;
  - a replay conflict leaves HEAD, index and files byte-identical;
  - dirty gives behind_dirty with the forecast and every file hash unchanged;
  - every skipped reason;
  - an untracked file colliding with the target gives changed_meanwhile and stays untouched;
  - crash recovery between the write-ahead and reset --keep (test fault); the backup ref exists;
  - marker/lock exclusion in both orders;
  - settle prints context only when something changed; settle with sync finishes within 15 s;
  - pre-push refuses trunk and cand refs, allows land refs, and is bypassed by HUB_GUARD=off; init chains an existing pre-push.

Files: packages/adapter/src/hooks.ts, guard.ts, mcp.ts (claim accepts path#Symbol), format.ts (denyReason with symbols, free keys and holds). Needs @agenthub/symbols from CP3a and hub H5. Read DESIGN 1.10 and 2.3.6. Build:
(1) pre-edit, for Edit or MultiEdit on an existing file in an enabled language: before = the file; after = symbols.applyEdit (applied in order for MultiEdit); diff = symbols.changedSymbols(path, before, after, {maxSymbols: 12}). The claim scope is the symbol entries with mapper, or files when the diff is file-level. Save before beside the inflight marker (cap 1 MiB).
(2) Deny reasons name the symbol, list the free keys (symbols.freeKeys), and say 'being landed by L-n' for holds. Write over a file where others hold symbols gets 'use Edit for the parts you change'.
(3) post-edit verification: re-read the file; if it differs from the simulated after, recompute changedSymbols(before, actual) and claim the missing keys; a denial becomes PostToolUse additionalContext.
